  "pronunciationText": "Here's one way to remember it. Think of the power, ay x plus b, as the playback speed of the curve. ay is the speed. Play it twice as fast, and the curve rises twice as fast at every height. Play it backwards, and it falls instead. b just starts the playback at a different point, so it adds no rate factor. And k makes the whole picture bigger, so heights and slopes grow together. In short, copy the exponential, then multiply by k and by ay."
